## STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] developer.vpbank.com (193.222.70.149) = SAME IP/front-end as www.vpbank.com (Apache+Envoy, shared session infra); PSD2 Berlin Group v1 sandbox API live and ANONYMOUS — `GET /psd2/berlin-group/v1/accounts` → HTTP 200 `{"accounts":[]}`, no client cert, no basic auth, no WAF interception.
- [NEW] TLS cert CN exposes openbanking.vpbank.com (193.222.70.154) = production PSD2 ASPSP; TLS-layered mTLS enforced — anonymous requests aborted with `tlsv13 alert certificate required`; properly locked.
- [NEW] Sandbox API sets `AL_SESS-S` bank session cookie on anonymous requests (same cookie as www Drupal).
- [NEW] PSD2 statistics XLSX (2024Q3–2026Q2) public on www.vpbank.com Drupal — uptime/PISP/AISP only, no endpoint intel.
- [CHANGED] developer.vpbank.com assessed as documented-open sandbox (release note 2024-05-06: basic auth creds removed from commands) — anonymous API access alone is NOT a reportable finding; its value is as a live logic-testing bed for the consent/payment state machine.

