**STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE**

Mass-assignment (conf 70 in prior lead) — I could not justify live testing: POST `{"user":{...admin/tenant_id}}` to `/api/v1/sessions` on a **production multi-tenant bank onboarding with customer PII** is a mutating/auth-bypass test against live customer data, explicitly prohibited by program rules. Dropping direct probe; reframing as the AUTH_HELPED force_tenant IDOR which only needs dev-stage creds (dev sandbox = synthetic). Not REJECTED — PARKED pending dev creds, but noting `/users/sign_up` 500 indicates registrable controller mounted on prod (a registration-enablement vector).

- [PARKED] Mass assignment via Devise sign_in on digital-onboarding prod: cannot test without mutating live customer auth flow; requires dev-stage creds. confidence 45 < resubmit-threshold without proof, reframed under force_tenant IDOR.
- [PARKED] ADFS device_code phishing: real path confirmed but blocks on client_id discovery (RAG surfaced only VP Bank Vietnam, separate entity).
- [PARKED] PSD2 sandbox BOLA → prod: HUMAN_ONLY (mTLS), confidence 35.
